## Track 1: Two Cents Above the Grain Line

**Story & Context:** At 96 BPM, Hana holds a stable washint tonic while Sami enters roughly two cents sharp. The natural beat is extremely slow, swelling over several seconds. Rui uses only kick, one clipped rim, and a short root sub pulse every two bars. As Sami widens the offset toward four cents, the acoustic beating becomes more noticeable and the rim disappears through Beat Handoff. Marta places one damped vibraphone fifth only after the Beat Field stabilizes. Yared marks the shift from SLOW to WALK with one woodblock strike. Nuno enters with a low muted trombone pedal during the first Zero-Line, when the two washints finally converge and the beating nearly vanishes.

**Visual & Lyrics Prompt:** Grain inspection card with one central tolerance line and two nearly parallel ochre marks, one drifting only slightly above the other; dust floating over a mechanical scale. Sparse vocal fragments limited to “two cents high,” “hold the center,” “grain line,” and “meet at zero.”

## Track 2: Parallel Flutes Cross at Bin Six

**Story & Context:** At 102 BPM, the track foregrounds Phase Crossing. Hana holds a fixed fifth while Sami begins below her pitch and rises almost imperceptibly. The natural beating accelerates as the pitches approach. Rui gradually removes hats and rim hits so the interference itself becomes the fast upper pulse. At the exact crossing point, the beating collapses for a brief instant; the drums also drop to kick only. As Sami continues above Hana, the beating reappears and widens into PULSE. Marta answers the crossing with a prepared-vibraphone suspended-second shell. Nuno remains silent until after the pitches have clearly separated again, then plays a short falling fourth.

**Visual & Lyrics Prompt:** Two parallel measurement lines on a grain-bin chart converging at BIN 6, touching at one point, then separating again; two flute silhouettes arranged like crossing survey marks. Sparse vocal fragments limited to “bin six,” “cross slowly,” “nothing at the center,” and “separate again.”

## Track 3: Zero Line After the Last Weighing

**Story & Context:** The closer runs at 88 BPM and begins almost without drums. Hana and Sami hold a low near-unison with a moderate WALK beat while Marta uses isolated vibraphone octaves and Yared plays only soft kebero rim taps. Rui enters with a short sub pulse after every fourth acoustic swell rather than on a fixed bar position. Over several minutes the players gradually reduce their tuning offset, making the beat slower and slower. Nuno adds breath-heavy bass-trombone pedals beneath the final approach. In the last minute, both washints reach Zero-Line and hold the most stable unison on the EP. Rui removes the sub entirely. The track ends with two dry flute tones, a faint shared room resonance, and no electronic cadence.

